BND-20: print 0 instead of NaN when no routing step falls in the reporting period

The status report divides by ReportStepCount and RoutingTimeSpan (Node Depth
average depth, Storage average volume, Outfall flow frequency, Flow
Classification fractions, Pump utilization) and the Groundwater Summary by
the runoff time, with no check for zero. With no routing step after
REPORT_START (the reporting window lies outside every [EVENTS] period, or a
toolkit client ends the run before the first swmm_step) these print -nan.
Divide by at least one step / one second: the accumulated statistics are
0 in that case, so the report shows 0. Also skip the non-convergence
frequency in stats_report() when no routing step was taken (0/0, no printed
value). Results with at least one step are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-20_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/stats.c b/src/legacy/engine/stats.c
index 6d38f70..f0a4fd2 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/stats.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/stats.c
@@ -795,7 +795,7 @@ void stats_findMaxStats()
     stepCount = TimeStepStats.timeStepCount;
 
     // --- find nodes with highest nonconvergence frequency
-    if ( RouteModel == DW )
+    if ( RouteModel == DW && stepCount > 0 )
         for (j = 0; j < Nobjects[NODE]; j++)
             stats_updateMaxStats(MaxNonConverged, NODE, j,
                 NodeStats[j].nonConvergedCount / stepCount);
